{#
    jumpNav(items, classes)
    - Sticky row of small pill anchor links that scroll down to sections further on the same
      page (e.g. right below a pageHero) — items: array of { text, url }, where url is a
      same-page hash like "#regiony". The target section needs a matching `id` (see
      contentSection's `id` param) and enough scroll-margin-top to clear this nav once it's
      stuck (plus the sticky header) — global smooth scrolling is set once on `html`.
    - Sticks to the top of the viewport on scroll (right below the sticky header at lg — see
      --header-height, kept in sync by main.js). While scrolling, the pill for whichever
      section is currently in view is highlighted and scrolled into view within this row
      (relevant once the row is wider than the viewport, e.g. on mobile) — see main.js's
      [data-jump-nav] handling.
#}
{% macro jumpNav(items=[], classes="") %}
{% if items.length %}
<nav class="{{ ["c-jump-nav", classes] | select | join(" ") }}" aria-label="Rychlá navigace na sekce stránky" data-jump-nav>
    <div class="c-container c-jump-nav__inner">
        {% for item in items %}
            <a href="{{ item.url }}" class="c-jump-nav__pill" data-jump-link>{{ item.text }}</a>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</nav>
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
